<div class="page">
  <h1 style="text-align: center; font-size: 18pt;">CONTRACT AGREEMENT</h1>
  <p>FOR CIP PROJECT:</p>
  <p>This Agreement made on this <span data-field="date_of_agreement">{{ date_of_agreement }}</span> day of <span data-field="month_of_agreement">{{ month_of_agreement }}</span>, <span data-field="year_of_agreement">{{ year_of_agreement }}</span>, between the University of Guam, whose address is <span data-field="university_address">{{ university_address }}</span>, (a Guam Corporation duly licensed Contractor), whose physical address is <span data-field="university_physical_address">{{ university_physical_address }}</span>, herein referred to as the "CONTRACTOR",</p>
  <p>The Contractor will be responsible for satisfying the scope of work identified in Section One; terms and conditions of this Agreement (including, but not limited to, the bonding requirements of the construction performance) in accordance with the bid request and bid proposal submitted the Contractor.</p>

  <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">SECTION ONE</h2>
  <h3 style="text-align: center;">DESCRIPTION OF WORK</h3>
  <p>The Contractor shall perform the following described work, in accordance with the plans and specifications attached and the bid proposal submitted by the Contractor:</p>
  <p>The plans, specifications, and communication as referred to herein are attached hereto and incorporated by reference.</p>

  <p>The plans and specifications referred to are as follows:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>University of Guam Bid Package, UOG BID</li>
    <li>Sealed Bid Price Proposal submitted by <span data-field="bid_submission_date">{{ bid_submission_date }}</span>.</li>
    <li>Other Reference Documents and Scope of Work provided in Bid package including Attachment K and Exhibits A, B, C, & D.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">SECTION TWO</h2>
  <h3 style="text-align: center;">STARTING AND COMPLETION DATES</h3>
  <p>The Contractor agrees to commence the work within <span data-field="start_date_period">{{ start_date_period }}</span> calendar days after receipt of this Agreement signed by the University President and issuance of written "Notice to Proceed" (NTP). Once the work is commenced, the Contractor shall be obligated to complete the work to the NTP. The Contractor shall commence said work thereafter closely following the NTP, and in any event to complete the same within <span data-field="completion_period">{{ completion_period }}</span> calendar days from the date of NTP. The Contractor shall provide the University with a written schedule of work place amendments on the site prior to receipt of Signed Agreement and issuance of written NTP from Owner.</p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">SECTION THREE</h2>
  <h3 style="text-align: center;">PRICE</h3>
  <p>Owner agrees to pay Contractor, for the work described, the total price of <span data-field="total_price">{{ total_price }}</span> dollars and <span data-field="cents_amount">{{ cents_amount }}</span> cents ( <span data-field="total_price_words">{{ total_price_words }}</span> ).</p>

  <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">SECTION FOUR</h2>
  <h3 style="text-align: center;">PROGRESSIVE PAYMENTS</h3>
  <p>Owner shall make progress payments to the Contractor, on the basis of applications for payment submitted to the University's Project Manager by the Contractor as the work progresses, and on the Project Manager's certificate thereof. Payments shall be made upon work completed and materials in place as certified by the Contractor on Standard AIA Document G702. Payments shall be made within <span data-field="payment_days">{{ payment_days }}</span> calendar days after final completion and is payable in accordance with Section Five herein. Any work deleted will be credited as per supplemental schedule.</p>

  <p>Progress payments may be withheld if:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Work is found defective and not remedied;</li>
    <li>The Contractor does not make prompt and proper payments to subcontractors;</li>
    <li>The Contractor does not make prompt and proper payments for labor, materials, or equipment furnished to him;</li>
    <li>Claims or liens are filed on the job; or</li>
    <li>In the opinion of Project Manager, the Contractor's work is not progressing satisfactorily.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>CONTRACT FOR UOG BID <span data-field="contract_id">{{ contract_id }}</span> CIP Project <span data-field="contractor_initials">{{ contractor_initials }}</span></p>
  <p>_________________________ <span data-field="owner_signature_line">{{ owner_signature_line }}</span> Page 1 of 14</p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">SECTION FIVE</h2>
  <h3 style="text-align: center;">FINAL PAYMENT</h3>
  <p>Owner shall make final payment to the Contractor within <span data-field="final_payment_days">{{ final_payment_days }}</span> calendar days after the work is finally completed and the Contractor has delivered to Owner a complete release of all liens arising out of the Agreement herein, or satisfactory documenting evidence of full payment covering all labor, materials, and equipment for which a lien could be filed, or in the alternative a bond satisfactory to Owner indemnifying it against such liens.</p>

  <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">SECTION SIX</h2>
  <h3 style="text-align: center;">DESIGNATION OF PROJECT MANAGER</h3>
  <p>The Project Manager for this project is <span data-field="project_manager_name">{{ project_manager_name }}</span>, <span data-field="project_manager_title">{{ project_manager_title }}</span>, <span data-field="project_manager_office">{{ project_manager_office }}</span> of the University of Guam. The duties and authority of the Project Manager are as follows:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>General Administration of Agreement: The primary function of the Project Manager is to provide the general administration of the Agreement. In performing these duties, he is the Owner's representative during the entire period of the Agreement.</li>
    <li>Inspection and Progress Reports: The Project Manager shall keep field records of the work, including the quality of work by making inspection visits to the work. He will make general progress reports to the Owner, and shall keep records of the work proceeding in accordance with the Agreement.</li>
    <li>Authority to Direct Work: The Project Manager shall have the authority to direct the work, and to instruct the Contractor on the manner in which the work is to be performed.</li>
    <li>Acceptance of Work: The Project Manager shall be the person who shall give final approval to the work performed by the Contractor.</li>
    <li>Acceptance of Work Site for Inspections: The Project Manager shall be given free access to the work at all times during its preparation and progress. The Contractor shall provide the Project Manager with reasonable access to the work site for inspection.</li>
    <li>Interpretation of Agreement: The Project Manager will be the initial interpreter of the Agreement requirements, and make primary decisions on claims and disputes between the Contractor and Owner. The Project Manager's decisions are subject to mediation and arbitration as provided in Section Thirteen of this Agreement.</li>
    <li>Review of Change Orders: The Project Manager shall review all proposed change orders and shall recommend approval or rejection to the Owner.</li>
    <li>Review of Change Orders: The Project Manager shall review all proposed change orders and shall recommend approval or rejection to the Owner.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">SECTION SEVEN</h2>
  <h3 style="text-align: center;">EQUIPMENT OPPORTUNITY</h3>
  <p>The Contractor has received a copy of the University of Guam's CIP Project. The Contractor warrants that neither in the delivery of its services nor in its employment practices will it discriminate against any individual on the basis of race, color, creed, national origin, sex, age, (except as permitted by law), disability, status as a special disabled Veteran status, or as a Veteran of the Vietnam Era or citizenship status (except as permitted by law) or any other status protected under the University's EEO policy or by law that will in timely and every respect with all provisions of federal and Guam law regarding this obligation. The Contractor agrees to indemnify and hold harmless the University of Guam, its agents, servants and employees from any and all claims arising out of any alleged failure on the part of the Contractor to honor this obligation.</p>

  <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">SECTION EIGHT</h2>
  <h3 style="text-align: center;">EMPLOYMENT RESTRICTIONS</h3>
  <p>The Contractor warrants that no person in its employment who has been convicted of a sex offense under the provisions of G CSA Chapter 25 or of an offense defined in G CSA Chapter 28, Article 2, or who has been convicted of an offense with the same elements as heretofore defined in any other jurisdiction, or who is listed on the Sex Offender Registry shall provide services on behalf of the Contractor while on University of Guam property. If any employee of the Contractor is providing services on University property and is convicted subsequent to an award of a contract, then the Contractor shall immediately remove such employee from University property and shall notify the University in writing within twenty-four (24) hours of the conviction. If the Contractor fails to remove such employee from providing services on University property within twenty-four (24) hours of the conviction, the University reserves the right to terminate the contract for cause. The Contractor shall take corrective action within twenty-four (24) hours of notice from the University, and the Contractor shall notify the University when action has been taken. If the Contractor fails to take corrective steps within twenty-four (24) hours of notice from the University, then the University in its sole discretion may suspend temporarily any contract for services until corrective action has been taken.</p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">SECTION NINE</h2>
  <h3 style="text-align: center;">WAIVER</h3>
  <p>The terms of this Agreement are severable such that any term or provision is declared by a court of competent jurisdiction to be illegal, void or unenforceable, the remainder of the provisions shall continue to be valid and enforceable.</p>

  <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">SECTION TEN</h2>
  <h3 style="text-align: center;">NOTICES</h3>
  <p>No waiver of performance by either party shall be construed as or operate as a waiver of any subsequent default of any terms, covenants or conditions of this Agreement.</p>

  <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">SECTION ELEVEN</h2>
  <h3 style="text-align: center;">OWNER'S PROJECT MANAGER</h3>
  <p>OWNER: UNIVERSITY OF GUAM</p>
  <p>Office of the President</p>
  <p>ATN: VP&A & Legal Office</p>
  <p>UOG Station, Mangilao, GU 96923</p>
  <p>Tel. No. (671) 735-2990/2900</p>
  <p>Tel. No. (671) 735-2990/2900</p>
  <p>OWNER'S PROJECT MANAGER: <span data-field="owner_pm_name">{{ owner_pm_name }}</span></p>
  <p>Title: <span data-field="owner_pm_title">{{ owner_pm_title }}</span></p>
  <p>Office: <span data-field="owner_pm_office">{{ owner_pm_office }}</span></p>
  <p>Location: <span data-field="owner_pm_location">{{ owner_pm_location }}</span></p>
  <p>E-mail: <span data-field="owner_pm_email">{{ owner_pm_email }}</span></p>
  <p>Tel. No.: <span data-field="owner_pm_phone">{{ owner_pm_phone }}</span> & Fax No.: <span data-field="owner_pm_fax">{{ owner_pm_fax }}</span></p>
  <p>CONTRACTOR: <span data-field="contractor_name">{{ contractor_name }}</span></p>
  <p>_________________________ <span data-field="contractor_signature_line">{{ contractor_signature_line }}</span></p>
  <p>SECTION TWENTY-ONE</p>
  <p>ENTIRE AGREEMENT; MODIFICATION</p>
  <p>This Agreement constitutes the entire agreement of the parties and supersedes any and all prior or contemporaneous representations or agreements, whether in written or oral, between the parties, and cannot be changed or modified unless in writing, signed by the parties.</p>
  <p>CONTRACT FOR UOG BID <span data-field="contract_id_bottom">{{ contract_id_bottom }}</span> CIP Project <span data-field="contractor_initial_bottom">{{ contractor_initial_bottom }}</span> Page 5 of 14</p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">SECTION TWENTY-TWO</h2>
  <h3 style="text-align: center;">A. CONTRACT CLAUSES FOR CONSTRUCTION CONTRACTS ONLY</h3>
  <p>NOTE: The President of the University of Guam is the University's Chief Procurement Officer and replaces any reference below to the Director of Public Works or the head of the Purchasing Agency. References to the "territory" or "territorial" shall mean the University of Guam.</p>

  <p>(1) Variations Requiring Adjustments. The quantity of any item in this contract is an estimated quantity and where the actual quantity of such item varies more than <span data-field="variation_percentage">{{ variation_percentage }}</span> percent above or below the estimated quantity stated in this contract, an adjustment in the contract price shall be made upon demand of either party. The adjustment shall be made in accordance with the provisions of this Agreement. If the actual quantity of such item varies more than <span data-field="variation_percentage_two">{{ variation_percentage_two }}</span> percent above or below the estimated quantity stated in this contract, an adjustment in the contract price shall be made upon demand of either party. The adjustment shall be made in accordance with the provisions of this Agreement.</p>
  <p>(2) Suspension of Work. The University may suspend the work at any time for any reason, including but not limited to, weather, labor disputes, or other causes beyond the Contractor's control. In the event of a suspension of work, the Contractor shall be entitled to compensation for the time lost due to the suspension, in accordance with the provisions of this Agreement.</p>
  <p>(3) Time Extension. If the work is delayed by any cause beyond the Contractor's control, the Contractor shall be entitled to an extension of time, provided that the Contractor shall notify the University in writing within <span data-field="notice_period_days">{{ notice_period_days }}</span> days of the occurrence of such delay. The extension of time shall be granted in accordance with the provisions of this Agreement.</p>
  <p>(4) Adjustments of Price. Any adjustment in contract price must persuade to this clause shall be determined in accordance with the Price Adjustment Clause of this contract.</p>

  <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">SECTION TWENTY-THREE</h2>
  <h3 style="text-align: center;">DIFFERING SITE CONDITIONS</h3>
  <p>If during the course of the work, the Contractor encounters differing site conditions, notify the Director of Public Works or the head of a Purchasing Agency of such conditions in writing. The Contractor shall be entitled to an adjustment in the contract price and/or an extension of time as provided in this Agreement.</p>

  <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">SECTION TWENTY-FOUR</h2>
  <h3 style="text-align: center;">CLAIMS BASED ON THE DIRECTOR OF PUBLIC WORKS OR THE HEAD OF A PURCHASING AGENCY'S ACTIONS OR OMISSIONS</h3>
  <p>(1) Notice of Claim. If any action or omission on the part of the Director of Public Works or the head of the Purchasing Agency, or designee of such, causes the Contractor to incur any costs or damages, the Contractor shall provide written notice to the Director of Public Works or the head of the Purchasing Agency within <span data-field="claim_notice_days">{{ claim_notice_days }}</span> days after the occurrence of such action or omission. Failure to provide such notice shall waive the Contractor's right to claim for such action or omission.</p>
  <p>(2) Claim Submission. The Contractor shall submit a detailed written claim within <span data-field="claim_submission_days">{{ claim_submission_days }}</span> days after the occurrence of such action or omission. The claim shall include all supporting documentation and shall be prepared in accordance with the requirements of this Agreement.</p>
  <p>(3) Resolution. The Director of Public Works or the head of the Purchasing Agency shall review the claim and shall respond in writing within <span data-field="response_days">{{ response_days }}</span> days. If the parties cannot reach a resolution, the claim shall be submitted to mediation as provided in Section Thirteen of this Agreement.</p>
  <p>(4) No Claim After Final Payment. No claim by the Contractor for an adjustment under these shall be allowed if asserted after final payment under this contract.</p>
  <p>(5) Knowledge. Nothing contained in this clause shall be grounds for an adjustment in compensation if the Contractor had actual knowledge of the existence of such conditions prior to the submission of bids.</p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">SECTION TWENTY-FIVE</h2>
  <h3 style="text-align: center;">PRICE ADJUSTMENT</h3>
  <p>(1) Price Adjustment Methods. Any adjustment in contract price pursuant to clauses in this contract shall be made in one or more of the following ways:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>(a) By agreement on a fixed price adjustment before commencement of the pertinent performance or as soon thereafter as practicable;</li>
    <li>(b) By unit prices specified in the contract or subsequently agreed upon;</li>
    <li>(c) By a formula specified in the contract or subsequently agreed upon; or</li>
    <li>(d) In such other manner as the parties may mutually agree; or</li>
  </ul>
  <p>(2) Price Adjustment by Owner. The Owner may, at its sole discretion, make any adjustment to the contract price, provided that the adjustment is in accordance with the provisions of this Agreement. The Owner may make such adjustment for any reason, including but not limited to, changes in scope, materials, labor, or other costs, provided that the adjustment is in accordance with the provisions of this Agreement.</p>
  <p>(3) Adjustment of Price. Any adjustment in the contract price made pursuant to this clause shall be determined in accordance with the Price Adjustment Clause of this contract.</p>

  <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">SECTION TWENTY-SIX</h2>
  <h3 style="text-align: center;">CLAIMS BASED ON THE DIRECTOR OF PUBLIC WORKS OR THE HEAD OF A PURCHASING AGENCY'S ACTIONS OR OMISSIONS</h3>
  <p>(1) Notice of Claim. If any action or omission on the part of the Director of Public Works or the head of the Purchasing Agency, or designee of such, causes the Contractor to incur any costs or damages, the Contractor shall provide written notice to the Director of Public Works or the head of the Purchasing Agency within <span data-field="claim_notice_days_2">{{ claim_notice_days_2 }}</span> days after the occurrence of such action or omission. Failure to provide such notice shall waive the Contractor's right to claim for such action or omission.</p>
  <p>(2) Claim Submission. The Contractor shall submit a detailed written claim within <span data-field="claim_submission_days_2">{{ claim_submission_days_2 }}</span> days after the occurrence of such action or omission. The claim shall include all supporting documentation and shall be prepared in accordance with the requirements of this Agreement.</p>
  <p>(3) Resolution. The Director of Public Works or the head of the Purchasing Agency shall review the claim and shall respond in writing within <span data-field="response_days_2">{{ response_days_2 }}</span> days. If the parties cannot reach a resolution, the claim shall be submitted to mediation as provided in Section Thirteen of this Agreement.</p>

  <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">SECTION TWENTY-SEVEN</h2>
  <h3 style="text-align: center;">TERMINATION FOR DEFAULT FOR NONPERFORMANCE OR DELAY - DAMAGES FOR DELAY - TIME EXTENSIONS</h3>
  <p>(1) Termination. If the Contractor fails to complete the work or any portion thereof, or any part thereof, with such diligence as will assure its completion within the time specified in this contract, or any extension thereof, the Owner may terminate the contract in whole or in part, and the Contractor shall be liable for all damages incurred by the Owner as a result of such termination.</p>
  <p>(2) Liquidated Damages. If and when liquidated damages are provided in the contract, and if the territory so permits, the Contractor shall pay to the Owner the sum of <span data-field="liquidated_damages_amount">{{ liquidated_damages_amount }}</span> for each day of delay, up to a maximum of <span data-field="liquidated_damages_cap">{{ liquidated_damages_cap }}</span>.</p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">SECTION TWENTY-EIGHT</h2>
  <h3 style="text-align: center;">LIQUIDATED DAMAGES</h3>
  <p>When the Contractor fails to complete the work or any portion of the work within the time or times fixed in the contract or any extension thereof, the Contractor shall pay to the Owner the sum of <span data-field="liquidated_damages_amount_2">{{ liquidated_damages_amount_2 }}</span> for each day of delay, up to a maximum of <span data-field="liquidated_damages_cap_2">{{ liquidated_damages_cap_2 }}</span>.</p>

  <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">SECTION TWENTY-NINE</h2>
  <h3 style="text-align: center;">TERMINATION FOR CONVENIENCE</h3>
  <p>The Project Manager may, when the interests of the University require, terminate this contract in whole or in part, for the convenience of the University. The Project Manager shall give written notice of the termination to the contracting party the date of termination and when termination becomes effective.</p>
  <p>(2) Contractor's Obligations. The Contractor shall continue to perform the work until the date of termination, and shall cooperate with the University in the orderly completion of the work. The Contractor shall also terminate all outstanding orders and subcontracts and orders contracted with the terminated work. The Project Manager shall direct the Contractor to assign the contractor's obligations to a successor contractor, and the Contractor shall cooperate with the University in the transition to the successor contractor.</p>
  <p>(3) Compensation. The Contractor shall be entitled to compensation for work performed, costs incurred, and reasonable demobilization costs, provided that the Contractor shall submit a written claim detailing these items within <span data-field="compensation_claim_days">{{ compensation_claim_days }}</span> days of the date of termination.</p>
  <p>(4) Compensation. The Contractor shall submit a termination claim specifying the amounts due because of the termination for convenience together with supporting documentation. The Project Manager shall review the claim and shall respond in writing within <span data-field="compensation_review_days">{{ compensation_review_days }}</span> days of receipt of the claim.</p>
  <p>CONTRACT FOR UOG BID <span data-field="contract_id_final">{{ contract_id_final }}</span> CIP Project <span data-field="contractor_initial_final">{{ contractor_initial_final }}</span> Page 8 of 14</p>
</div>




<div class="page">
  <p style="text-align: justify;">
    (2) The Procurement Officer and the contractor may agree to a settlement provided the contractor has filed a termination claim supported by cost or pricing data submitted as required by <span data-field="reference_section_2_1">{{ reference_section_2_1 }}</span> of the Guam Procurement Regulations and that the settlement does not exceed the total contract price plus settlement costs reduced by payments previously made by the territory, the proceeds of any sales of construction, supplies, and construction materials under Paragraph (3) of this clause, and the contract price of the work not terminated.
  </p>
  <p style="text-align: justify;">
    (3) Absent complete agreement under Subparagraph (b) of this Paragraph, the Procurement Officer shall pay the contractor the following amounts, provided payments under Subparagraph (b) shall not duplicate payments under this Paragraph: (i) with respect to all contract work performed prior to the effective date of the notice of termination, the total (without duplication of any items of); (ii) the cost of such work plus a fair and reasonable profit on such portion of the work (such profit shall not include anticipatory profit or consequential damages) less amounts paid or to be paid for completed portions of such work provided, however, that the contractor would have sustained a loss if the entire contract had been performed, no profit shall be allowed or included and the amount of compensation shall be reduced to reflect the loss; (iii) cost of setting and claiming paying all remaining out of the termination of subcontractors or orders pursuant to Paragraph (2) of this clause. These costs must not include costs paid in accordance with Subparagraph (c) (ii) of this Paragraph.
  </p>
  <p style="text-align: justify;">
    (c) The reasonable settlement costs of the contractor including accounting, legal, clerical, and other expenses reasonably necessary for the preparation of settlement claims and supporting data with respect to the terminated portion of the contract and for the termination and settlement of subcontractors thereof, together with reasonable storage, transportation, and other costs incurred in connection with the protection or disposition of property allocable to the terminated portion of this contract. The total sum to be paid under this Paragraph shall not exceed the total contract price plus the reasonable settlement costs of the contractor reduced by the amount of any sales of construction, supplies, and construction materials under Paragraph (3) of this clause, and the contract price of work not terminated.
  </p>
  <p style="text-align: justify;">
    (d) Cost claimed, agreed to, or established under Subparagraph (b) and (c) of this Paragraph shall be in accordance with Chapter 7 (Cost Principles) of the Guam Procurement Regulations.
  </p>
  <h3 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">REMEDIES</h3>
  <p style="text-align: justify;">
    Any dispute arising under or out of this contract is subject to the provisions of Chapter 9 (Legal and Contractual Remedies) of the Guam Procurement Regulations.
  </p>
  <h3 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">B. CONTRACT CLAUSES FOR NON-CONSTRUCTION CONTRACTS, IF APPLICABLE</h3>
  <p style="text-align: justify;">
    NOTE: The President of University of Guam is the University's Chief Procurement Officer and replaces any reference below to the Director of Public Works or the head of the Purchasing Agency. References to "territory" or "territorial" shall mean the University of Guam.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h3 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">CHANGES</h3>
  <p style="text-align: justify;">
    (1) Change Order:
  </p>
  <p style="text-align: justify;">
    By a written order, at any time, and without notice to the surety, the Chief Procurement Officer or the head of a Purchasing Agency may, subject to all appropriate adjustments, make changes within the general scope of this contract in any one or more of the following:
  </p>
  <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
    <li>(a) Drawings, designs, or specifications, if the supplies to be furnished are to be specially manufactured for the territory in accordance therewith;</li>
    <li>(b) Method of Shipment or packaging; or</li>
    <li>(c) Place of Delivery</li>
  </ul>
  <p style="text-align: justify;">
    (2) Adjustments of Price or Time Performance:
  </p>
  <p style="text-align: justify;">
    If any such change order increases or decreases the contractor's cost of, or the time required for performance of any part of the work under this contract, whether or not changed by the order, an adjustment shall be made and the contract modified in writing accordingly. Any adjustment in contract price made pursuant to this clause shall be determined in accordance with the Price Adjustment Clause of this contract. Failure of the parties to agree to an adjustment shall not excuse the contractor from the with the contract as changed, provided that the territory promptly and duly make such provisional adjustments in payment or time for performance as may be reasonable. By proceeding with the work, the contractor shall not be deemed to have accepted any change order for additional compensation or an extension of time for completion.
  </p>
  <p style="text-align: justify;">
    (3) Time Period for Claim:
  </p>
  <p style="text-align: justify;">
    Within 30 days after receipt of a written change order under Paragraph (1) (Change Order) of this clause, unless such period is extended by the Procurement Officer in writing, the contractor shall file notice of intent to assert a claim for an adjustment. Later notification shall not bar the contractor's claim unless the territory is prejudiced by the delay in notification.
  </p>
  <p style="text-align: justify;">
    (4) Claims Barred After Final Payment:
  </p>
  <p style="text-align: justify;">
    No claim by the contractor for an adjustment hereunder shall be allowed if notice is not given prior to final payment under this contract.
  </p>
  <p style="text-align: justify;">
    (5) Other Claims Not Barred:
  </p>
  <p style="text-align: justify;">
    In the absence of such a change order, nothing in this clause shall be deemed to restrict Contractor's right to pursue a claim arising under the contract if pursued in accordance with the clause entitled, "Claims Based on a Procurement Officer's Actions or Omissions, Notice of Claim Clause," or breach of contract.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h3 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">STOP WORK ORDER</h3>
  <p style="text-align: justify;">
    Order to Stop Work. The Procurement Officer may, by written order to the contractor, at any time, and without notice to any surety, require the contractor to stop all or any part of the work called for by this contract. This order shall be for a specified period of time, and the contractor shall promptly comply with this order. If the contractor fails to comply with this order, the contractor shall be deemed in default of this contract. Upon receipt of such order, the contractor shall forthwith comply with its terms and take all reasonable steps to minimize the occurrence of costs allocable to the work covered by the order during the period of work stoppage. Before the stop work order expires or within any further period to which the parties shall have agreed, the Procurement Officer shall either
  </p>
  <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
    <li>(A) Cancel the stop work order; or</li>
    <li>(B) Terminate the work covered by such order as provided in the "Termination for Convenience Clause" of this Contract.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">VARIATION IN QUANTITY</h3>
  <p style="text-align: justify;">
    Upon the agreement of the parties, the quantity of supplies or services or both specified in this contract may be increased by a maximum of ten percent (10%); provided:
  </p>
  <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
    <li>(A) The unit prices will remain the same (except for any price adjustment provisions applicable); and</li>
    <li>(B) The Procurement Officer makes a written determination that such an increase will either be more economical than awarding another contract or that it would not be practical to award another contract.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">PRICE ADJUSTMENT</h3>
  <p style="text-align: justify;">
    Any adjustments in contract price made pursuant to this clause shall be determined in accordance with the Price Adjustment Clause of this contract.
  </p>
  <p style="text-align: justify;">
    (1) Price Adjustment Methods. Any adjustment in contract price pursuant to this contract shall be made in one or more of the following ways:
  </p>
  <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
    <li>(a) by agreement on a fixed price adjustment before commencement of all the pertinent performance or as soon thereafter as practicable;</li>
    <li>(b) by unit prices specified in the contract or subsequently agreed upon;</li>
    <li>(c) by the costs attributable to the event or situation covered by the clause, plus appropriate profit or fee, as all specified in the contract or subsequently agreed upon; or</li>
    <li>(d) in such manner as the parties may mutually agree; or</li>
  </ul>
  <p style="text-align: justify;">
    (2) Submission of Cost or Pricing Data. The contractor shall submit cost or pricing data for any price adjustments subject to the provisions of <span data-field="reference_section_2_2">{{ reference_section_2_2 }}</span> of the Guam Procurement Regulations.
  </p>
</div>

